 "narrative": "All newly delivered results were assessed against the same pragmatic scale-relevant benchmark for these mostly negative dependency scores: approximately 10% of absolute mean magnitude, about 0.0093 for outcome_006 and outcome_014, 0.0269 for outcome_013, 0.0282 for outcome_008, 0.0301 for outcome_011, and 0.0415 for outcome_001. Because these estimates are already signed to the hypothesis direction, positive values support the claimed direction and negative values oppose it. Cell counts satisfy the minimum-20 rule, nominal categories are treated as labels rather than ordered numbers, and no leakage or coding convention problem is evident. The main limitation is multiplicity: these are many unadjusted screening tests, so acceptance requires an interval entirely on the clinically meaningful side of the benchmark, not merely a point estimate or a marginal zero-excluding interval.\n\nThe conditional tests refining earlier leads do not support clinically meaningful marker-absent effects. H151 tests feature_052 on outcome_006 among feature_021=0; R145 has a small positive signed estimate +0.0061 with CI [-0.0162, +0.0284], including negligible, zero, and opposite-direction values, so I reject and close. H152 tests feature_042 on outcome_014 among feature_027=0; R146 is -0.0011 with CI [-0.0215, +0.0194], essentially null and not supportable. H153 tests feature_065 on outcome_014 among feature_027=0; R147 is +0.0160, exceeding the 0.0093 benchmark at the point, but its CI [-0.0059, +0.0378] includes zero, clinically negligible values, and opposite-direction modification of the claimed direction, so it is unsupported after multiplicity and uncertainty and is closed.\n\nThe two feature_024 median-split interaction tests H154 and H155 are also non-supportive. H154 tests whether feature_024 high status increases the accepted positive feature_021 effect on outcome_006; R148 is -0.0090 with CI [-0.0486, +0.0306], including zero and clinically negligible modification. H155 tests analogous modification of feature_027 on outcome_014; R149 is -0.0070 with CI [-0.0473, +0.0334]. These are consistent with stability of the two central associations rather than evidence for a clinically meaningful subgroup modification.\n\nThe final broad binary screens H132-H136 all fail to support claimed positive associations for outcome_013, outcome_008, outcome_011, and outcome_001 with feature_034 or feature_002. R150 through R154 all have signed point estimates below or opposite the relevant benchmarks and intervals crossing zero or negligible values. I reject and close H132, H133, H134, H135, and H136. These nulls make a new broad binary marker unlikely, though they do not prove absence for every untested predictor.\n\nIn the modifier family for the accepted feature_021-outcome_006 association, H126 is rejected: R156 is -0.0024 with CI [-0.0511, +0.0464], far from a supportable positive modification. H124 is the only new nondecisive signal: R155 is +0.0289 with CI [-0.0150, +0.0728], a positive point above the outcome_006 benchmark but an interval that still includes zero, negligible modification, and clinically meaningful opposite modification. I leave H124 unresolved rather than accepted or fully closed because it is a potential modifier of a large supported marker effect. However, I do not request validation for it yet: its prior is weakened by the failed independent validation of the related feature_009 main-effect lead H119, by the large number of interaction screens, and by the very wide discovery interval. An independent validation at the stringent run-wide alpha may not resolve it unless the true modification is much larger than currently estimated. I activate H125, H127, and H128 to complete the same feature_021 interaction family; if those are null, H124 will be much more plausibly a chance lead and should be closed. If any produces a robust positive interval beyond benchmark, I will use validation capacity on that stronger candidate. The supported supplied-dataset landscape remains unchanged: feature_021=1 is associated with much higher outcome_006 scores, and feature_027=1 is associated with much higher outcome_014 scores. These are dataset-internal associations only, not causal or externally generalizable claims.",
 "research_notes": "Round 12 appraise updates. New conditional/interaction screens H151-H155 and final binary screens H132-H136 are rejected/closed; none provides interval-level evidence beyond the scale-relevant 10% benchmark. H126 is rejected. H124 remains unresolved and active as a nondecisive positive feature_021-by-feature_009 interaction (R155 +0.0289 CI [-0.0150,+0.0728]) but is not validated now because it is weak, multiple-test-prone, and related feature_009 main effect failed validation. To contextualize H124, activate H125, H127, and H128 for remaining feature_021 interaction tests. Next analyze should prioritize H125/H127/H128. If they are null, reject H124 and close the feature_021 modifier family unless a new candidate emerges. If one produces a strong interval excluding negligible effects, request validation. Accepted landscape remains: H89/H93/H94 feature_021=1 -> much higher outcome_006; H39/H95/H96 feature_027=1 -> much higher outcome_014. All conclusions are supplied-dataset associations, not causality or generalizability."
